{
  "name": "16_syn_retransmission",
  "description": "a SYN re-sent twice with no payload \u2014 the count must fire while the byte counter stays 0",
  "derivation": "a SYN consumes one sequence number, so eff_len = 1 and the packet IS seq-bearing. p1 sets the high-water mark to 501. p2 and p3 reuse seq=500 and end at 501 <= 501, so both are retransmissions. Their payload is 0, so retrans bytes = 0 and log_tcp_retrans_bytes = log1p(0) = 0.0 while log_tcp_retrans_count = log1p(2). This is the documented count-vs-bytes distinction: control-plane retransmission at no data cost.",
